---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="The Crimes — Long Knife"
  description="Pollution, climate destruction, and a century of killings. The crimes the Kochs and Big Oil committed on the Osage Reservation — and how they made them legal."
>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       CRIME ONE — POLLUTION
       Rhythm: cinematic opener → two-col text → single full-bleed
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="pollution">

    <!-- Cinematic title card: 85vh, title bottom-left -->
    <div class="relative h-[85vh] min-h-[560px] w-full">
      <img
        src="/still-pumpjack-sunset.jpg"
        alt="A pump jack silhouetted against a smoky amber sunset on the Osage Reservation."
        class="absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover"
        loading="eager"
      />
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-[var(--color-ink)] via-black/10 to-transparent"></div>
      <div class="absolute bottom-0 left-0 px-10 pb-16 sm:px-16 lg:px-20 lg:pb-20">
        <p class="text-[10px] tracking-[0.55em] text-[var(--color-red)] uppercase">Crime One</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 font-[family-name:var(--font-display)] text-[clamp(4rem,10vw,8rem)] leading-[0.88] tracking-tight text-white">
          Pollution<br/>Crimes
        </h2>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Two-column body text: left col heavier, right col lighter -->
    <!-- All body text left-aligned — narrative reads left to right -->
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-5 px-10 py-20 sm:px-16 sm:py-24 lg:px-20 lg:py-28 gap-10 md:gap-16">
      <div class="md:col-span-3 space-y-6 text-left text-base leading-relaxed text-white/75 sm:text-lg">
        <p>
          Charlie Koch didn't steal all the Osage oil. Some his crews dumped into creeks and rivers.
          Koch let pipes crack, spewing murderous poisons. Koch Oil was indicted for over
          <strong class="text-[var(--color-bone)] font-medium">315 counts of felonious criminal polluting</strong>.
          And walked away smelling like a rose.
        </p>
        <p>
          We reveal the inside story of how Koch bought and bullied his way out of these crimes &mdash;
          from having Koch thugs impersonate an FBI agent to terrorize a whistleblower, to running
          counterintelligence operations against the Feds, to slipping millions through &ldquo;Triad,&rdquo;
          a corporate front.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="md:col-span-2 flex flex-col justify-start space-y-6 text-left text-base leading-relaxed text-white/60 sm:text-lg md:pt-0">
        <p>
          How did he get away with it? The Kochs bought themselves a Congress and pleasured a Supreme
          Court Justice. And they simply had Congress and the Court
          <em class="text-white/80 not-italic font-medium">make their crimes legal</em>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Single full-bleed image — the visual full stop -->
    <figure>
      <img
        src="/koch-warning-sign.jpg"
        alt="A weathered Koch high-pressure petroleum warning sign fallen in the brush."
        class="h-[62vh] w-full object-cover sm:h-[75vh]"
        loading="lazy"
      />
    </figure>
  </section>


  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       CRIME TWO — CLIMATE
       Rhythm: stat statement → chapter title + text → portrait + quotes
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="climate">

    <!-- Stats anchored inside the chapter title block, not floating alone -->
    <!-- Left: numbers. Right: chapter title + body. Gives the stats context immediately. -->
    <!-- Single centered column — title, stats, body all share one axis -->
    <div class="px-10 py-24 sm:px-16 sm:py-32 lg:py-40 text-center flex flex-col items-center">
      <p class="text-[10px] tracking-[0.55em] text-[var(--color-red)] uppercase">Crime Two</p>
      <h2 class="mt-4 font-[family-name:var(--font-display)] text-[clamp(3.5rem,9vw,7.5rem)] leading-[0.88] tracking-tight text-white">
        Climate<br/>Crimes
      </h2>

      <!-- Stats inline below title, side by side, centered -->
      <div class="mt-16 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-center gap-12 sm:gap-20 lg:gap-28">
        <div class="text-center">
          <p class="font-[family-name:var(--font-display)] text-[clamp(3rem,7vw,5.5rem)] leading-none tracking-tight text-[var(--color-red)]">
            16,000
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-[11px] tracking-[0.25em] text-white/45 uppercase leading-relaxed max-w-[160px]">
            Abandoned wells spewing methane on Osage land
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block w-px h-16 bg-white/10"></div>
        <div class="text-center">
          <p class="font-[family-name:var(--font-display)] text-[clamp(3rem,7vw,5.5rem)] leading-none tracking-tight text-[var(--color-red)]">
            8,000%
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-[11px] tracking-[0.25em] text-white/45 uppercase leading-relaxed max-w-[160px]">
            More damaging to the climate than CO₂
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Body text centered, constrained width for readability -->
      <p class="mt-16 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-white/70 sm:text-lg">
        After Koch and Big Oil &mdash; Getty, Sinclair and Exxon &mdash; sucked billions in petroleum
        from the Osage Reservation, they left the Tribe with 16,000 abandoned wells spewing chemicals
        and methane. There is nothing worse for the climate than methane.
      </p>
    </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Portrait (3 cols) + two quotes stacked (2 cols) -->
    <div class="md:grid md:grid-cols-5 md:items-stretch">
      <figure class="relative min-h-[55vw] md:col-span-3 md:min-h-[600px]">
        <img
          src="/still-county-clerk.jpg"
          alt="A subject interviewed at the Land Records County Clerk office."
          class="absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover object-center"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </figure>
      <div class="md:col-span-2 flex flex-col justify-center gap-12 px-10 py-16 sm:px-14 lg:px-16 lg:py-20">
        <!-- Quotes centered — these are spoken words, testimony, not narrative prose -->
        <blockquote class="text-center">
          <p class="font-[family-name:var(--font-quote)] text-[clamp(1.2rem,2.2vw,1.7rem)] leading-snug text-white italic">
            &ldquo;Now how do you allow a company to just walk away like that?&rdquo;
          </p>
          <cite class="mt-4 block text-[10px] tracking-[0.35em] text-white/35 not-italic uppercase">
            — Everett Waller, Osage Minerals Council
          </cite>
        </blockquote>

        <div class="h-px bg-white/8"></div>

        <!-- Standing Bear: centered, Bebas for weight, attribution centered below -->
        <div class="text-center">
          <p class="font-[family-name:var(--font-display)] text-[clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem)] leading-[1.1] tracking-tight text-white">
            &ldquo;Let's not beat around the bush.
          </p>
          <p class="font-[family-name:var(--font-display)] text-[clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem)] leading-[1.1] tracking-tight text-[var(--color-red)]">
            This is occupied territory.&rdquo;
          </p>
          <p class="mt-5 text-[10px] tracking-[0.45em] text-white/35 uppercase">
            — Principal Chief Geoffrey Standing Bear
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       CRIME THREE — KILLERS OF THE FLOWER MOON
       Rhythm: cinematic opener → text (2-col) → full-bleed → typography close
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="flower-moon" class="mt-1">

    <!-- Cinematic title card — Kihekah trio now opens Crime Three -->
    <div class="relative h-[80vh] min-h-[500px] w-full">
      <img
        src="/still-kihekah-trio.jpg"
        alt="Three figures — two Osage elders and a white official — standing outside the Kihekah building."
        class="absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover object-center"
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-[var(--color-ink)] via-black/20 to-transparent"></div>
      <div class="absolute bottom-0 left-0 px-10 pb-16 sm:px-16 lg:px-20 lg:pb-20">
        <p class="text-[10px] tracking-[0.55em] text-[var(--color-red)] uppercase">Crime Three</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 font-[family-name:var(--font-display)] text-[clamp(2.8rem,7vw,6rem)] leading-[0.88] tracking-tight text-white">
          The Crimes of the<br/>Killers of the<br/>Flower Moon
        </h2>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Two-column intro: both left-aligned, matched padding -->
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 px-10 pt-20 pb-16 sm:px-16 sm:pt-24 sm:pb-20 lg:px-20 lg:pt-28 lg:pb-24 gap-10 md:gap-20">
      <p class="text-left text-base leading-relaxed text-white/75 sm:text-lg">
        In the 1870s, starvation and smallpox killed 90% of the tribe. After oil was discovered,
        by 1919 the Osage had become, per capita, the richest people in the world.
        Then the killings began.
      </p>
      <p class="text-left text-base leading-relaxed text-white/75 sm:text-lg">
        <em class="text-[var(--color-bone)] not-italic">Long Knife</em> is the documentary
        sequel to <cite>Killers of the Flower Moon</cite> &mdash; the Martin Scorsese masterpiece
        about the 200 Osage murdered for their oil. We uncover hard new facts about this Reign of Terror.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Full-bleed skull testimony headline -->
    <figure>
      <img
        src="/still-skull-testimony.jpg"
        alt="Archival newspaper headline: Skull Is Shown As Testimony In Osage Case."
        class="h-[65vh] w-full object-cover object-center sm:h-[78vh]"
        loading="lazy"
      />
    </figure>

    <!-- A Century of Theft — full width, body left, closing line centered -->
    <div class="px-10 pt-24 pb-32 sm:px-16 sm:pt-28 sm:pb-40 lg:px-20 lg:pt-36 lg:pb-48">
      <div class="space-y-12">
        <div>
          <p class="text-[10px] tracking-[0.55em] text-[var(--color-red)] uppercase">A Century of Theft</p>
          <div class="mt-5 h-px w-8 bg-white/12"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-7 text-left text-base leading-relaxed text-white/65 sm:text-lg">
          <p>
            History is ever-present. The crimes of the Kochs were foretold in the Trail of Tears,
            which ended with the Osage expulsion from Kansas after robber baron Jay Gould convinced
            Congress to let him buy the Osage reservation for just
            <strong class="text-white/85 font-medium">12 cents an acre</strong>. It was a scandal even then.
          </p>
          <p>
            In Oklahoma, Chief Bigheart wrote down their Constitution &mdash; democratically elected Chief,
            all land held in common. Congress revoked it, replaced Bigheart with a council of oil men,
            and chopped the land into 2,000 parcels. The easier to steal and cheat the Osage out of their
            oil. And to kill those who resisted.
          </p>
          <p>
            For a century, until 2006, the oil men ruled over the Osage. J. Paul Getty became the
            richest man in the world from the oil land he bought from the Osage for $500.
          </p>
          <p>
            The Kochs invented nothing new.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </section>

</Base>
